# reelplanner in a shared repo (the plan-to-video skill's "Several people"): add these lines to the repo's
# own .gitignore. A plan folder carries only its videos' text (BRIEF.md, STORYBOARD.md, SCRIPT.md, the
# frames' HTML, plan-map.json); the built video (its voice, images, fonts and captures) never enters git's
# history. A PR's built video goes, packed, on a branch of its own, video/pr-<n>, that is never merged and is
# deleted when the PR closes. (.reelplanner/.gitignore, from `reel init`, already leaves out each video's
# snapshots/, renders/ and voice, and every guide.) `reel pr-check` fails a PR that adds a voice file, an image
# or a video under .reelplanner/plans/.
.reelplanner/plans/*/*video/assets/
.reelplanner/plans/*/*video/capture/
.reelplanner/plans/*/*video/audio_meta.json
.reelplanner/plans/*/*video/audio_engine_meta.json
# an explainer (explain-first step 5, D-249): its text goes into git (explain.md, sources.json, the storyboard,
# script and frames, its reviews), never a transcript or its built video (voice, images, captures)
.reelplanner/explainers/*/video/assets/
.reelplanner/explainers/*/video/capture/
.reelplanner/explainers/*/video/audio_meta.json
.reelplanner/explainers/*/video/audio_engine_meta.json
# what each reviewed version was built from that nothing makes again (its screenshots and captured text), kept small
# and committed so `reel rebuild` can build it again: never ignore these
!.reelplanner/media/**
!.reelplanner/**/versions/**

# And in the repo's .gitattributes, so two branches' waiting memory lines are both kept when they merge:
#   .reelplanner/you.pending.jsonl merge=union
